---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { personLd, paperLd } from '../lib/schema';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';

const experience = [
  {
    title: 'High-performance cockpit platform · Tier-1 supplier',
    period: '02/2026 – present',
    bullets: [
      'Ported an Android infotainment product to Android 15 / AAOS as a guest on Xen and QNX hypervisors on a new automotive SoC (AOSP device targets, Soong / Kleaf).',
      'Brought up Android 15 and Linux guests on Xen and QNX Hypervisor: guest configurations, device-tree overlays, and passthrough of memory ranges, interrupts, clocks and pin control between domains.',
      'Adapted the evaluation-board BSP to the A-sample hardware: device-tree fixes, GPIO hogs, USB 2.0 controller and passthrough, boot-chain flashing (ATF, U-Boot, Xen), and the EVS camera HAL adapted to the new camera’s frame format.',
      'Debugged hardware and BSP issues on the bench; root-caused a silent UART in the Android guest on QNX Hypervisor to missing SoC support in the guest kernel’s GPIO driver, and added it.',
      'Created the Yocto build for the cluster Linux: a custom layer adding Qt 6 and cluster apps, a build-orchestration script and board image targets.',
      'Owned the Bluetooth bring-up of a UART-attached Wi-Fi / Bluetooth combo radio: UART passthrough between domains, device-tree nodes and a mainline driver backport into the Android Linux kernel; validated on hardware.',
      'Root-caused third-party app crashes (JNI reference-table overflow, heap exhaustion) from logcat and tombstones.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Central ADAS ECU · German OEM',
    period: '08/2024 – present',
    bullets: [
      'Developed AUTOSAR Classic switch CDD (Complex Device Driver) features in C on a multi-core safety microcontroller for a dual-die automotive Ethernet switch: a data-path-reset DTC, a UDS crash-dump routine, and a DLT redesign that cut log bandwidth with no data loss.',
      'Owned switch configuration as sole engineer across every specification release, both dies and all variants (TCAM, VLAN, QoS, AVB, port mirroring); built a PyQt6 simulator of the switch frame pipeline.',
      'Maintained the MACsec part of the CDD; root-caused lost error history (the switch clears entries on read) and a missing DTC caused by a queue delay.',
      'Implemented DEM freeze frames and a security DTC derived from JTAG-lock and secure-boot states, configuring AUTOSAR ports, runnables, events and task mapping.',
      'Designed a Vector CANoe stress-test framework: a simulated switch node in CAPL, Python code generators, and a C++ OpenSSL library for AES key wrap and AES-CMAC; its tests found real CDD defects, and the team adopted it as a template.',
      'Set up the CUnit-based unit-test environment under Bazel and designed tests to MC/DC coverage for ASPICE SWE.4.',
      'Integrated OEM AUTOSAR platform and HSM releases; root-caused an HSM memory-window shift blocking ECU coding, an NvM write failure and log drops from MTU overflow.',
      'Supported ISO 26262 ASIL B work: automated PIL / SIL results, closed gaps against the MCAL safety manual’s assumptions of use, and fixed MISRA C (QAC) and CodeSonar findings.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Bluetooth / Wi-Fi over Ethernet · motorcycle OEM',
    period: '10/2026 – 11/2026',
    bullets: [
      'Architected a two-ECU design for wireless phone projection with the radio on an AUTOSAR Classic ECU: SOME/IP services covering every proxy operation, a connection policy manager, and an IPsec-protected GRETAP Wi-Fi path.',
      'Built and hardware-tested the ESP32 proof of concept: C firmware (ESP-IDF, FreeRTOS, Bluedroid Classic + BLE, OTA), a BlueZ-compatible D-Bus facade, and a virtual-time simulation model verified by scenario and unit tests.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'R&D and AI engineering · eJad',
    period: '02/2025 – present',
    bullets: [
      'Initiated a multi-agent LLM approach for ASPICE SWE.4 unit-test generation, shortening unit-test development and reducing VectorCAST generation effort.',
      'Rewrote the tool in Python as sole author: an agentic LangGraph pipeline with self-correcting build / test / coverage loops, task-based routing across Gemini, DeepSeek and local Ollama models, and a PySide6 GUI.',
      'Added SWE.5 integration-test generation, extended the team’s VectorCAST RAG generator (LangChain, FAISS) with new LLM providers and an offline mode, and built GitHub Copilot agents and skills that turn test specifications into CUnit suites.',
      'Evaluated SDV platforms: an ADAS showcase on Eclipse S-CORE (Bazel, zero-copy IPC), Eclipse OpenBSW cross-compiled, flashed and debugged on NXP S32K148 (GCC, Rust), and the navigation stack of a team Qt 6 / QML cluster demo.',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base jsonLd={[{ '@type': 'ProfilePage', mainEntity: personLd(Astro.site) }, paperLd(Astro.site)]} ogType="profile" title="Resume" description="Resume of AbdElrahman Khalil, embedded software engineer: AUTOSAR Classic, embedded Linux and Android under hypervisors, AI-assisted test engineering.">
  <div class="top">
    <div>
      <h1>Resume</h1>
      <p class="muted">{profile.role} · {profile.location}</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href={profile.resumePdf} download={profile.resumePdfName}>Download PDF</a>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>Embedded software engineer with 2+ years on automotive OEM and Tier-1 projects. Platform bring-up of Android 15 (AAOS) and Linux guests under Xen and QNX on new automotive SoCs: BSP adaptation, kernel drivers, device trees, Yocto. Embedded C on AUTOSAR Classic: an Ethernet switch CDD, UDS diagnostics, MACsec and unit testing under ASPICE and ISO 26262. Builds multi-agent LLM tools that write and fix unit tests.</p>

    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <p class="role-line"><strong>Embedded Software Engineer, {profile.employer}</strong> <span class="mono muted">07/2024 – present</span></p>
    {experience.map((e) => (
      <section class="job">
        <h3>{e.title} <span class="mono muted period">{e.period}</span></h3>
        <ul>{e.bullets.map((b) => <li>{b}</li>)}</ul>
      </section>
    ))}

    <h2>Academic project</h2>
    <section class="job">
      <h3>Driver monitoring system on TI TDA4VM · graduation project funded and mentored by eJad <span class="mono muted period">2024</span></h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Real-time camera-based driver monitoring on BeagleBone AI-64 (TI TDA4VM) classifying driver state from eye closure, gaze, yawning and head pose.</li>
        <li>IMX219 IR sensor over MIPI CSI-2 / V4L2 on embedded Linux (device-tree overlays); a GStreamer + TIOVX (OpenVX) pipeline offloading pre-processing to the vision pre-processing accelerator (VPAC) and C66x DSPs, optimised to run in real time.</li>
        <li>An x86 software-in-the-loop environment simulating the TDA4VM cores, imager and DSPs for CI and dataset-based testing.</li>
        <li>Co-author: <a href={profile.paper.url}>{profile.paper.title}</a>, IEEE MIUCC 2024.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/projects/driver-monitoring-tda4vm/">Case study →</a></p>
    </section>

    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <ul class="skills">
      <li><strong>Languages:</strong> C, C++, Python, Bash, CAPL, QML, Rust (basic), MATLAB.</li>
      <li><strong>Embedded Linux and Android:</strong> Linux kernel drivers, device trees and overlays, Yocto, BSP and board bring-up, boot chain (ATF, U-Boot), UART, GPIO, USB, BlueZ, D-Bus, GStreamer, V4L2, Xen, QNX Hypervisor, AOSP / AAOS (Android 15), Android HAL.</li>
      <li><strong>Automotive and embedded:</strong> AUTOSAR Classic / OSEK, Complex Device Drivers, RTE, MCAL, DEM / DCM, UDS, NvM, DLT, SOME/IP, HSM / secure boot, FreeRTOS, ISO 26262 (ASIL B), ASPICE, MISRA C.</li>
      <li><strong>MCUs and SoCs:</strong> multi-core safety MCUs, automotive cockpit SoCs, NXP S32K148, ESP32, ATmega32, TI TDA4VM.</li>
      <li><strong>Networking:</strong> Automotive Ethernet (TCAM, VLAN, QoS, AVB), MACsec, TCP/IP, IPsec, Bluetooth Classic / BLE, Wi-Fi, Wireshark.</li>
      <li><strong>Testing:</strong> CUnit, pytest, MC/DC, LCOV / gcov, VectorCAST, Vector CANoe, PIL / SIL, QAC, CodeSonar.</li>
      <li><strong>AI / LLM:</strong> LangGraph, LangChain, RAG (FAISS), prompt and context engineering, reflection loops, multi-provider model routing, Gemini / Vertex AI, DeepSeek, Ollama, GitHub Copilot agents and skills.</li>
      <li><strong>Tools:</strong> Git, Gerrit, Bazel, CMake, Docker, Jira, Qt 6 / PySide6, Altium, Eagle, OrCAD.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p><strong>B.Sc. in Communication and Electronics Engineering</strong>, Alexandria University, 2019 – 2024. Courses: Embedded Systems (ITI), Visual Embedded Android (AOSP), AI course (Tech Pathways MENA).</p>

    <h2>Leadership</h2>
    <p>Chairman, IEEE Alexandria Student Branch (2023–2024) · Hardware Engineer, ROBO-TECH (2022–2024) · PR Head, Success Training Programs (2021–2023) · Mentor, eJad graduation-project team (2026). <a href="/about/">Details →</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .top { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; gap: var(--space-4); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: var(--space-5); margin-bottom: var(--space-5); }
  .top h1 { margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }
  .top p { margin: 0; }
  .job h3 { font-size: var(--text-base); margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .period { font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--text-sm); white-space: nowrap; }
  .role-line { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .skills { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
</style>
